@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.819 = private unnamed_addr constant [600 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for redundant `Final[Literal[...]]` annotations.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAll constant variables annotated as `Final` are understood as implicitly\0Ahaving `Literal` types by a type checker. As such, a `Final[Literal[...]]`\0Aannotation can often be replaced with a bare `Final`, annotation, which\0Awill have the same meaning to the type checker while being more concise and\0Amore readable.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Afrom typing import Final, Literal\0A\0Ax: Final[Literal[42]]\0Ay: Final[Literal[42]] = 42\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Afrom typing import Final, Literal\0A\0Ax: Final = 42\0Ay: Final = 42\0A```\0A", align 1
