@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.936 = private unnamed_addr constant [615 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for lambda expressions which are assigned to a variable.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APer PEP 8, you should \22Always use a def statement instead of an assignment\0Astatement that binds a lambda expression directly to an identifier.\22\0A\0AUsing a `def` statement leads to better tracebacks, and the assignment\0Aitself negates the primary benefit of using a `lambda` expression (i.e.,\0Athat it can be embedded inside another expression).\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Af = lambda x: 2 * x\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef f(x):\0A    return 2 * x\0A```\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#programming-recommendations\0A", align 1
