@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.959 = private unnamed_addr constant [728 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for dictionary iterations that extract the dictionary value\0Avia explicit indexing, instead of using `.items()`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIterating over a dictionary with `.items()` is semantically clearer\0Aand more efficient than extracting the value with the key.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0AORCHESTRA = {\0A    \22violin\22: \22strings\22,\0A    \22oboe\22: \22woodwind\22,\0A    \22tuba\22: \22brass\22,\0A    \22gong\22: \22percussion\22,\0A}\0A\0Afor instrument in ORCHESTRA:\0A    print(f\22{instrument}: {ORCHESTRA[instrument]}\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0AORCHESTRA = {\0A    \22violin\22: \22strings\22,\0A    \22oboe\22: \22woodwind\22,\0A    \22tuba\22: \22brass\22,\0A    \22gong\22: \22percussion\22,\0A}\0A\0Afor instrument, section in ORCHESTRA.items():\0A    print(f\22{instrument}: {section}\22)\0A```\0A", align 1
