@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.1048 = private unnamed_addr constant [1010 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for generator expressions, list and set comprehensions that can\0Abe replaced with `itertools.starmap`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen unpacking values from iterators to pass them directly to\0Aa function, prefer `itertools.starmap`.\0A\0AUsing `itertools.starmap` is more concise and readable. Furthermore, it is\0Amore efficient than generator expressions, and in some versions of Python,\0Ait is more efficient than comprehensions.\0A\0A## Known problems\0ASince Python 3.12, `itertools.starmap` is less efficient than\0Acomprehensions ([#7771]). This is due to [PEP 709], which made\0Acomprehensions faster.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aall(predicate(a, b) for a, b in some_iterable)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom itertools import starmap\0A\0A\0Aall(starmap(predicate, some_iterable))\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `itertools.starmap`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/itertools.html#itertools.starmap)\0A\0A[PEP 709]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0709/\0A[#7771]: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/7771\0A", align 1
